            <ArticleTitle>Fatal polyarteritis nodosa with massive mesenteric necrosis in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Polyarteritis nodosa (PAN) is a rare vasculitic syndrome in childhood. There are few reported cases of ischaemic necrosis of the intestine and even fewer survivors in adults. We report the case of a 10-year-old boy with PAN and an acute abdomen that required operative intervention. Evidence was found of mesenteric arteritis with large ischaemic segments resulting in infarction and perforation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
